          # "Item starting with a blank line": the marker and its whitespace run
          # reach the end of the line, so the item has no first child HERE to
          # classify — and nothing is left to recurse ON. Reading only LM_CHARS
          # against the line length missed it, because LM_CHARS is zero in that
          # fallback rather than the whole line: `substr(s, 1)` handed back the
          # SAME string and the recursion never terminated. A `+ ` line in a
          # canonical doc then hung the check or overflowed the awk stack
          # instead of producing a verdict, so the guard is a hang, not a
          # misclassification. LM_CHARS <= 0 is held alongside the flag so any
          # future path that returns without a first child fails safe the same
          # way.
