      # It is stripped ONCE, here, rather than absorbed by the whitespace
      # classes downstream — which is what used to happen, invisibly, while
      # those classes were [[:space:]]. Narrowing them to the ASCII set the
      # spec actually defines therefore broke CRLF documents until this line
      # existed: a CRLF "blank" line stopped reading as blank, a fence closer
      # with a trailing CR stopped closing its fence, and a link after that
